Subject: [PATCH] model: inkling2_loop shares the scales with its loop slots

This is ggml-org/llama.cpp pull request 32704 by Daniel Han (danielhanchen),
"model : inkling2_loop re-share the loop slots after the scale pass", as it
stood on 2026-11-21: open, on 29b52d398, not merged. Carried here until a pin
has it; drop this file then.

inkling2_loop gives every later pass through its core layers cache slots of
their own and copies the physical layers into them (load_arch_tensors) before
load_tensors attaches the scale tensors (blk.N.ffn_down_exps.scale,
blk.N.ffn_gate_up_exps.scale). The copies kept null scales, so the second and
third pass ran the NVFP4 experts unscaled. The pull request gives a perplexity
of 130.43 for such a file against 7.65 with the scales. The file Unsloth
publishes for mainline (Mainline_Support/Inkling-2-Mini-UD-Q2_K_XL) has 20
scale tensors of each kind, so it needs this; a file without scale tensors is
not affected.

diff --git a/src/llama-model.cpp b/src/llama-model.cpp
index 4c77f6f68..914ba9f17 100644
--- a/src/llama-model.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-model.cpp
@@ -2006,6 +2006,12 @@ bool llama_model_base::load_tensors(llama_model_loader & ml) {
                 layer.nextn.shared_head_head_in_s = create_tensor(tn(LLM_TENSOR_NEXTN_SHARED_HEAD_HEAD, "input_scale", i), {1}, TENSOR_NOT_REQUIRED);
             }
         }
+        // inkling2_loop: the cache slots copied the physical layers before the scale pass, re-share them
+        if (auto * lm = dynamic_cast<llama_model_inkling2_loop *>(this)) {
+            for (int il = lm->n_phys; il < n_layer_all; ++il) {
+                layers[il] = layers[lm->layer_phys(il)];
+            }
+        }
         // output scales
         if (output) {
             // weight scale
